# --- Legacy WordPress oEmbed endpoints ------------------------------------
# WordPress served an iframe-able embed card at /embed/ (front page) and at
# /{post}/embed/. The *.html entries below are not real WordPress URLs — they
# were manufactured by a bug on this site's own 404 page, which used relative
# links, so a crawl of /embed/ turned "contact.html" into /embed/contact.html
# and so on. That bug is fixed (404.html and js/main.js now emit root-relative
# URLs); these rules retire the URLs Google already has on file.
/embed/                                     /                              301
/embed/index.html                           /                              301
/embed/contact.html                         /contact                       301
/embed/get-started.html                     /get-started                   301
/embed/warehouse-services.html              /warehouse-services            301
/embed/safe-secure-art-storage.html         /safe-secure-art-storage       301
/embed/convention-storage.html              /convention-storage            301
/embed/cross-docking.html                   /cross-docking                 301
/embed/small-local-moves-and-storage.html   /small-local-moves-and-storage 301
/embed/*                                    /                              301

# --- Legacy WordPress archives and custom post types ----------------------
# Author, category, and tag archives have no equivalent on the static site;
# the blog index is the closest real listing page. /project/* was a custom
# post type used for work samples, which the services overview now covers.
/author/*   /blog               301
/category/* /blog               301
/tag/*      /blog               301
/project/*  /warehouse-services 301

# Note: /wp-content/uploads/* is deliberately NOT redirected. Those media
# files were not carried over and have no equivalent, so 404 is the correct,
# honest response — redirecting images to an HTML page would just convert the
# 404s into soft 404s. Google drops them on its own once they stop resolving.
